# Seiche's speed dial (physics catalog plan, 2026-10-03): slow motion on the
# fixture (tree.html?physics_speed=0.2). Over the last thirty frames the
# drawing moves on every one while the simulation steps on fewer, and the
# canvas reports 0.2x. Time owed is wall time, so the share of frames that
# step is 0.2 x the frame interval over a tick: one in five only at 60 Hz
# (the canvas's native receipt holds that exactly).
assert snap ready == true
assert snap physics-speed == 0.2
click role:button Play physics
settle 2
assert snap physics-paused == false
click role:combobox Arrangement
settle 1
click role:option Free (physics alone)
settle 1
click role:button Apply arrangement
settle 1
assert snap layout == free
settle 40
log-physics slow
assert snap physics-effective-speed >= 0.15
assert snap physics-effective-speed <= 0.25
assert snap pace-frames == 30
assert snap pace-drawn-moved == 30
assert snap pace-stepped >= 3
assert snap pace-stepped <= 20
assert snap finite == true
log p6 speed slow receipt complete
